# PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

MAYOR OF PALANGKA RAYA

CENTRAL KALIMANTAN PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF PALANGKA RAYA CITY

NUMBER 1 OF 2021

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

MAYOR OF PALANGKA RAYA,

Considering:

a. that every citizen has the right to survival, growth, and proper development and to obtain consistent and systematic security as a form of Protection for Women and Children as mandated in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
b. that the Regional Government, families, groups, social organizations and/or other community organizations have responsibility for the implementation of fulfillment, protection, respect, advancement and prevention of rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. that to provide direction, legal basis and legal certainty in the Protection of Women and Children, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to stipulate a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In view of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 5 of 1965 concerning the Establishment of Kotapradja Palangka Raya (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1965 Number 48, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2753);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on the Elimination of all Form of Discrimination Against Woman) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as last amended by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
6. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
8. Law Number 52 of 2009 concerning Population Development and Family Development (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 161, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5080);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
11. Government Regulation Number 59 of 2019 concerning Implementation of Child Protection Coordination (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2019 Number 160, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6382);
12. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 532);
13. Regional Regulation of Palangka Raya City Number 17 of 2013 concerning Child Protection in the Context of Realizing a Child-Friendly City (Regional Gazette of Palangka Raya City of 2017 Number 17, Supplement to the Regional Gazette Number 8);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF PALANGKA RAYA CITY

and

MAYOR OF PALANGKA RAYA

HAS DECIDED:

To stipulate:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

# CHAPTER I

## GENERAL PROVISIONS

#### Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:
1. Region is Palangka Raya City.
2. Regional Government is the Mayor as an element of the Regional Government administration who leads the implementation of government affairs that are the authority of the autonomous region.
3. Mayor is the Mayor of Palangka Raya.
4. Regional Apparatus hereinafter abbreviated as PD is an auxiliary element of the Mayor and the Regional House of Representatives in the administration of government affairs that are the authority of the Region.
5. Protection of women is all efforts aimed at protecting women and providing a sense of security in the fulfillment of their rights by providing consistent and systematic attention aimed at achieving gender equality.
6. Child protection is all activities to guarantee and protect Children and their rights so that they can live, grow, develop, and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and dignity, and receive protection from violence and discrimination.
7. Violence is any act that results in misery or suffering physically, psychologically, sexually and/or neglect, including threats to commit acts, coercion, or deprivation of liberty by law.
8. Woman is a person who is female.
9. Child is a person who is not yet 18 (eighteen) years old who is not married, including a child who is still in the womb.
10. Community is individuals, community groups, including parents and families.
11. Prevention is all efforts to eliminate all risks and adverse impacts of violence against women and children.
12. Child-Friendly City hereinafter abbreviated as KLA is a conducive community in developing all social psychological potential of a person optimally.
13. Child's Obligation is everything that must be carried out by children according to the function and role of children.
14. Forum for Handling Victims of Violence Against Women and Children hereinafter abbreviated as FPK2PA is a coordination forum for handling victims of violence against women and children whose implementation is tiered at the city and sub-district levels.
15. Integrated Service Center for Women's Empowerment and Children hereinafter abbreviated as P2TP2A is an integrated service center in efforts to empower women in various fields of development, as well as protection of women and children from various types of discrimination, and acts of violence, including trafficking in persons established by the regional government or community-based.
16. Child-Friendly Village hereinafter abbreviated as KRA is the development of a village area that unites the commitment and resources of the village government that involves the community and the business world in the village in order to promote, protect, fulfill and respect children's rights, which are planned consciously and sustainably.

